# Continuing past the landing site, as far as the rules allow.
#
# `play.4x` walks the first five steps of the loop and stops with territory 1 working every
# extractor it has room for and territory 2 claimed. This carries on: hold both, grow the
# second, and send the next pioneer out.
#
# It stops well short of the loop's last three steps, and not for want of a script. `C-11`:
# the model still discards metal and energy at the end of every turn, and the specification
# stopped saying that several proposals ago. Until the two agree, a play-through here would
# be measuring rules the release no longer has - so this goes as far as it goes, and the
# rest of `R-6` waits.

# Turn 10. Territory 1 is complete and pays for itself. Territory 2 has one farm at density
# six, so its single citizen becomes two.
work 3 extractor 1 food
work 3 extractor 1 metal
work 3 extractor 1 energy
work 1 extractor 2 food
end turn

# Turn 11. Two citizens in territory 2: one holds the food, one has nothing to spend metal
# on yet - a second farm needs a metal that territory 2 cannot make, having no mine and no
# way to build one until it has metal. That is the same bootstrap the landing site was
# spared by arriving with three extractors, and a pioneer does not carry them.
work 3 extractor 1 food
work 3 extractor 1 metal
work 3 extractor 1 energy
work 1 extractor 2 food

# The landing site can afford another pioneer every turn: two metal and six energy against
# twelve of each.
produce pioneer 1
end turn

# Turn 12. The second pioneer crosses to territory 3.
work 3 extractor 1 food
work 3 extractor 1 metal
work 3 extractor 1 energy
work 1 extractor 2 food
move pioneer 3
work 1 extractor 3 food
end turn
